WEBVTT

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.950
Spice And Wolf II

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.220
Well, at any rate, Nora,

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:12.640
I can't help thinking that encountering
you was indeed divine intervention.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.730
If it wasn't for you, I wouldn't have
this tipsy smile you see before you.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:21.280
I'm really grateful to
you as well, Lawrence.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.240
I'm glad I met you.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.890
No, I'm the one who's...

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.350
No, I'm the one...

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:31.210
On top of that, I made you help
me out in a crazy gold smuggling job.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.170
To be honest, I never
thought you'd accept the job.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.600
Neither did I. I never thought I'd accept it.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.990
What?

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:43.200
I'm strange, aren't I?

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:52.730
I'd been thinking that I'd definitely have
to do a radical thing like that some day.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.210
I thought I couldn't be
dependent on the church forever.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:59.880
So I'm deeply indebted to you, Lawrence.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.390
I'm not so great.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.610
Merchants are egotistical.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:08.950
If that's the case, it's
the same for me... perhaps.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:14.070
Are you drinking, Holo?

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.730
Do not worry about me.
I am just drinking on my own.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.940
Why don't you join us in
our conversation, Holo?

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Huh?

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.260
What? Are you already drunk?

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.080
I am the wise wolf who, it's
been said, would drink up a lake.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.790
There is no way I would get drunk
on such a small amount, is there?

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:32.490
Okay!

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:33.070
Huh?!

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:36.080
You heard her, let's
leave her alone for a while.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.090
What? But...

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.020
After I drink a little more,

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.020
I will join your conversation spontaneously.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.330
Just wait until then.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.800
Then, I'll wait.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.100
So what were we talking about?

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:47.850
All right, the food's here.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.930
Whoa! They look good!

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.810
Thank you very much.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:53.750
Would you like to eat some, too?

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.260
Do not bother. I am doing as I like, so...

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.900
I thought you said you
would leave me alone for a while.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:58.900
Oh yeah, I did.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:00.910
So what were we talking about?

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:04.570
Let's see... Was it about our encounter?

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.350
Oh? What was before that?

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.560
Ah, we were talking about sheep and rock salt.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.580
Oh yes, that's right.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.430
Well, I didn't know sheep can find rock salt.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:19.820
Yeah, they like salt very much, so...

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.340
For example, if you rub salt lightly on a rock,

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.720
they'll keep licking it forever.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.390
Then, I wonder if that story is true, too.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.630
What story is that?

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:34.670
I've heard about this torture using sheep
that's performed in some eastern town.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.730
I thought that couldn't be true, but...

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:38.990
Torture using sheep?

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:41.900
Yes. It's hilarious.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.460
They tie criminals up
and rub salt on their feet.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.700
And then they'd bring the sheep there.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:47.190
Ah!

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.370
Rub salt on their feet, huh?

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:57.130
Ah?!

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.460
I will remember this along with my anger.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.920
Sorry...

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.760
If they rub salt on
their feet, the sheep would...

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.940
They would lick them frantically, wouldn't they?

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:06.930
Probably...

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:11.840
Then, at first, the criminals
laugh like crazy because it tickles.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.210
I'm gonna die! I'm gonna laugh to death! Stop it!

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.410
That's a strange torture.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.120
Yeah, it is indeed unusual.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:22.160
There's no way the sheep would be satisfied just with that.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.450
They keep licking the bottoms of his feet and in the end...

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.820
what do you think would happen?!

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:28.410
What happened?!

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.980
All the criminal thought about was laughing

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:34.340
and he ended up spreading his wonderful smile to people.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:37.390
And they lived happily ever after.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.460
Is that a real story?

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.920
I made up the last part just now.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:44.710
Oh, you're silly, Lawrence.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.400
But up to that point, it's a true story.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.860
Who knows what goes on in the minds of sheep.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:53.240
Come to think of it, I don't know what to do

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.660
when they want to lick my
hands after I eat dried meat.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.010
They're good sheep, but, how should I put it...

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:02.490
I get a little scared since
they get too carried away.

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:06.210
In that respect, the knight
you're with seems obedient.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:06.740
What?

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:07.640
Ah...

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:12.140
Enek works so hard that he sometimes
becomes stubborn and inflexible, too.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.070
I'm sorry.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.330
Well, he really is well-trained.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:26.900
It must be because you're
quite a skilled shepherd.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:28.900
Not really...

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:33.300
Hm?

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:34.840
What's the matter?

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.130
Are you already drunk?

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:38.020
I am not drunk.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:41.460
How are you not drunk like that?
What will I do with you?

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:48.200
There is no way I would get drunk
on just three cups of alcohol, is there?

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:50.870
Ah, Holo...

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:51.660
Ah...!

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:57.990
I wonder if it is because I had been by myself in
wheat fields for hundreds of years up until recently.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:00.800
Every day went by peacefully.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.870
Yesterday was no different from today.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.960
Tomorrow was no different from
the day after tomorrow, either.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.720
Time only moved forward a few times
a year, as if it just remembered to do so.

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:11.450
The harvest festival once a year.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.550
The sowing festival twice a year.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:16.020
The festival to pray for no rain.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.020
And the festival to pray for no wind.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.130
The rest was a chunk of boring time...

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.940
ordinary days with no festivals being held.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.780
There were even times where
I watched a sapling become a huge tree.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.890
Compared to that, while traveling, every day is a new experience. It is like being reborn each day.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.670
The time that I spent with that young peddler

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:41.420
was only a few months but it was worth several decades.

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.460
We would have a clamorous fight in the morning

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.460
but reconcile by lunchtime.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:50.050
I would tease him by making him clean
off the bread crumbs from my mouth.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.320
We would have another fight over food at dusk

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:55.800
and calmly discuss the
following day's affairs at night.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:59.850
I have had several experiences
traveling and living with others.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:04.060
However, I do not have
time to remember those things.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.570
What was my partner doing yesterday?

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.670
What was he like this morning?

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:12.170
I am too busy thinking about these things.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:17.240
It was only at the beginning that I sobbed
while relaxing and remembering my home.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:23.810
Every day is full of excitement.
I cannot even feel sad in peace.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:26.210
It would be a lie if I said it is not fun.

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:29.130
Rather, it even worries
me since it is too much fun.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.360
Heavy...

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:37.220
Why am I in the inn?

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:43.980
Wh-What was that?!

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:47.200
If that really happened, it is the
biggest blunder in my whole life!

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:50.080
It was just a nightmare.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.090
I will forget it ever happened.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.800
I wonder why...

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:00.760
I carelessly become off guard
in front of that dumb face of his.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.270
When I do not like things,
I get angry. When it is funny, I laugh.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.440
I show him the side of me that is
completely unbecoming the wise wolf.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.400
After all, this is it.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:21.310
I can quickly react to enemies' attacks at any time in this position. This is suitable for me.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:26.660
In that respect, my partner
is fully exposing his dumbness.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:29.660
He is as if a stupid cat.

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:32.740
Well, one may have to be
defenseless and insensitive like him

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:35.450
in order to survive in the human world.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:41.740
Why is he not here?

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.760
To think that he is not by my
side at a critical time like this...

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:46.760
What a useless male he is.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.230
Why am I...

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:15.930
You are finally back. I am gla...

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:18.610
Why didn't you tell me
you were under the weather?

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.480
Uhm, well...

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:21.890
You're not a child.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:24.350
Don't tell me you didn't notice it until you fainted.

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:28.710
What were you going to do if
this should happen while traveling?

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:31.530
You may not understand this,

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:34.780
but if you fall sick in a forest or
wasteland, it could lead to death.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.000
I was really worried.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:41.750
I am sorry.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:43.200
So how're you feeling?

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:46.430
It is not a big deal.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:48.330
I think the exhaustion has
caught up with me. That is all.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:51.440
It's not, uhm... a special
disease or anything, right?

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:53.630
Do not worry.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.710
I see. Good.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:57.900
I'm really relieved now.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:59.890
Boy do you overreact.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:04.300
Well, when I thought about this and that,
all sorts of worries started swirling in my head.

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:08.220
It could be... Ah... It might be...

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.460
What is it? Tell me.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:14.350
Ah, well, I thought it could
be because you ate onions.

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:15.460
Huh?!

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.230
I am not a dog.

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:20.680
Yeah.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:22.520
You're the wise wolf, aren't you?

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:29.660
But it is too bad that I was not able
to enjoy the precious alcohol and feast.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.330
I'm a merchant, you know.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:33.250
I'm on the ball.

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:36.410
I asked them to wrap up the leftovers.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:37.820
Really?!

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:40.250
Yeah. I'll serve them to you right away.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:41.230
Yep, yep.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:42.570
So I want to say, but...

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:46.830
As I thought, you do have a fever.

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:49.080
Weren't you quite exhausted?

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:53.010
It is your fault!

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:53.810
Huh?

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:59.630
Your fingers are a little hard so they
are similar to the tip of a wolf's nose.

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:03.330
When wolves rub their noses,
to humans that would mean...

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:05.850
I cannot say it.

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:07.650
What the heck?

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:08.910
Nothing!

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.040
Forget it!

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.390
In any case, you have to wait on your food.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.000
Just take it easy and rest.

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:41.350
Lawrence!

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:54.890
It feels warm.

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.320
Holo, are you up?

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.920
Can you not tell?

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:10.990
How're you feeling?

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:12.180
I cannot get up.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:14.070
Really?

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:18.580
Indeed... you look as pale as
a princess from a good family.

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.490
But I am hungry.

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:22.070
That's a relief.

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:24.580
Well then, I'll ask the inn people
to make porridge or something.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.210
I am thirsty, too.

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:29.600
Is that water?

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:31.050
Ah... Well...

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:33.760
since you had a fever last night, I got some hard cider.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:34.280
Really?!

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.580
H-Hey, are you okay?

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:43.970
I wish you'd be even half
as quiet as you are now.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:47.000
You would get upset if I become quiet
and sleep in the wagon, would you not?

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:50.250
It wouldn't be fair if I was
the only one who's up, would it?

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:55.450
If I stay quiet, you would
eat more during the meals.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:57.570
I'm bigger than you are so that's just natural.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:00.780
Then to compete with you, I should act big, huh?

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:06.730
What's the matter?

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:08.380
The taste is...

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:10.100
Oh yeah, I diluted it.

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.160
You diluted it too much!

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.540
I thought that my nose stopped working.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.440
Diluted hard cider works
well when you have a fever.

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:19.370
Hm?

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.910
You don't know this sort of thing?

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.960
I am the wise wolf.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:28.240
I know there are lots of things that I do
not know in this world. I know that much.

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:33.870
Sicknesses happen when the
balance inside your body breaks down.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:35.670
It's like the ebb and flow of the tide.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.990
And, when that balance breaks down,

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:41.780
you cure it by adjusting
the four states of humans.

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:43.300
Four states?

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:44.180
That's right!

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:48.180
Being hot, cold, dry and moist. Those four.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.070
And...?

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:52.900
These things can be adjusted by food.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:57.280
Since you had a fever,
eating cold food is ideal.

00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:59.420
That's why apples are good.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:02.570
I would have liked raw apples.

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:03.950
Those won't work.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:07.900
Apples are cold, but they're dry.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:11.850
Those who're under the weather
are dry, so they need moisture.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:14.380
Because of that, it has
to be something to drink.

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:17.240
If that's the case, if you
drink alcohol, you'll feel good.

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:21.420
But strong alcohol is hot so
we need to lighten its strength.

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:25.710
So what else am I allowed to eat?

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:29.570
Yeah. If you got a fever
from accumulated fatigue,

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.480
you need to cool it down first.

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:35.360
Also, your body is probably dry,
so you need to gain back moisture.

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:40.830
But moisture cools down your body and
if you get too cold, you become gloomy.

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:45.170
Considering all that, how about taking
wheat porridge cooked in sheep's milk

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:49.340
and adding some apple
pieces and goat cheese to it?

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:52.120
Yes! I like that!

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:53.630
I want to eat that!

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:55.630
Hey...

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:58.510
Aren't you actually completely recovered?

00:15:58.510 --> 00:15:59.930
Hm... I feel dizzy.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:00.630
Ah! Holo!
Hm... I feel dizzy.

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.390
Please hurry up.

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:05.970
Well then, wait a little, okay?

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:08.310
Make sure you make a lot of porridge!

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:32.100
Lawrence!

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:54.850
Can you get up?

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:56.830
Hmm... I cannot.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:04.320
If I fall sick, you are going
to return the favor, right?

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.080
Yes, if you do not mind the Yoitz approach.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:09.420
I'll think about it.

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:14.490
Do not worry! I have a good nose.

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:18.120
I will do something about it
before you become like me.

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:21.160
I'm sorry that I didn't notice.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:24.380
But if possible, I'd like you
to tell me about it as well.

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.220
In any case, I seem to be
slow on these things, so...

00:17:29.030 --> 00:17:31.180
Yes... It seems like it would take a while for you to pick up on it

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:33.470
even when I get a sickness
that even doctors cannot cure.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:34.340
Hm?

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:36.170
Nothing.

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:37.690
More importantly, food please!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.440
If you can eat this much, you should be okay.

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:43.960
You'll probably recover
by tomorrow or the next day.

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.670
Ah... yes...

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:48.520
Once we leave this town, we'll
be on the wagon again for a while.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:51.660
I am sorry.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.240
Take your time and recuperate.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:58.250
I already gave up on traveling
hurriedly when I picked you up.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:02.270
Besides, after a storm comes a calm.

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:05.800
I gained back my reputation,
and it's actually even better.

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:09.510
When I think about that benefit, it's
okay to delay our departure by 2-3 days.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:13.230
There're more places that I'd like to go, so...

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:13.470
Huh?

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:15.720
The inn is... uhm...

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:18.940
too quiet, so...

00:18:19.940 --> 00:18:21.710
Hmm, true.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:28.380
At any rate, let's have a long talk about
tonight's dinner for a certain glutton, shall we?

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:30.010
That's your reason?!

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:31.740
Do you have a rough idea as to what you want?

00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:36.860
Though I said I'd like to have a long talk, I won't
be able to prepare it once the market is closed, so...

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:39.170
H-Hmm...

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:42.200
You look more or less fine, but
you still shouldn't eat heavy stuff.

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:43.350
What about meat?

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:46.660
No, you can't. Either porridge
or soup with bread dipped in.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:47.330
Hmm...

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.630
Then, that thing I ate earlier.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:51.090
Was it sheep's milk?

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:54.070
The sweet scent and the strong taste were good.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:55.270
I want that one!

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:56.970
Sheep's milk, huh?

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.820
Is there any problem?

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:02.310
Since it goes bad easily, the price of
decent milk goes up in the afternoon.

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:04.660
You want it to be fresh, right?

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:05.700
Of course!

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.440
Then shall we ask Nora to find some again?

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:11.700
She isn't a shepherd for nothing.
She's quite a good jud...

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:14.780
Ah... Uhm...

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:17.870
If we ask Nora, we can get good milk, so...

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:22.370
If you use the power of money,
you do not need that girl to get the milk, do you?

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:24.960
Th-That might be true, but...

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:26.380
But what?!

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.510
Wh... Why do you hate Nora so much?

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:34.010
What?

00:19:35.010 --> 00:19:36.840
Wh-What did you just say?

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:38.470
W-Well, uhm...

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:41.850
I don't know what happened between you and shepherds.

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:45.350
I understand that you don't
like her since you're a wolf.

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:48.860
But you don't have to show
your hostility that openly, do you?

00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:51.810
You see, she's very good-natured.

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:53.730
There's always an exception to the rule.

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.230
You know...

00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:58.740
Wh-What is it?

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:00.450
I am sorry.

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:02.730
So you get it?

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:04.950
Uhm... well, how should I put it...

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:05.860
Hm?

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:07.670
Oh well...

00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:09.550
you are that kind of person.

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:10.280
What?

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:11.880
I am counting on you to get good sheep's milk.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.560
Hm?

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:37.780
Nora came to see how you're doing.

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:39.550
How're you doing?

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:40.660
Ah...

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:45.160
Well, I just felt fatigued. That is all.

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:51.550
But I want someone to talk to.

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:55.760
May I ask something that
I have always wanted to ask?

00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:56.550
What?

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:57.180
Ah, sure.

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.500
I'll answer if I can...

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:02.890
What is the greatest trick to leading sheep?

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:04.090
What?

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:09.170
Hmm...

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:15.700
To have a big heart.

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:32.550
It's getting windy, isn't it?

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:35.300
You are right.

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:36.390
Huh?

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:39.930
Sheep are convinced that they are clever, so...

00:21:40.930 --> 00:21:42.430
Are you talking about something interesting?

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.210
N... Not really.

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:44.670
Huh?

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:47.950
It is a secret between women.

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:50.150
Yeah?

00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:52.150
Huh?

00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:06.500
Wolf And Amber Melancholy

00:23:42.050 --> 00:23:43.080
Next episode...

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:44.750
Wolf And The Inadvertent Rift
